    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.6, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"short_to_supply\", \"components\": [\"U4\"], \"pins\": [\"U4.10\"], \"nets\": [\"VCC\"], \"observed\": \"U4 pin 10 (BS0) is wired onto the same horizontal bus as the VCC supply symbol and the pull-up resistors R4, R6 and R7 (junctions at the top of the bus). BS0 is therefore tied to VCC rather than to GND.\", \"expected\": \"BS0 should be strapped to GND, so that BS2/BS1/BS0 = 0/1/0 selects the I2C interface mode that the rest of the display circuit (D0 as SCL, D1/D2 as SDA) assumes.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`BS0` (pin 10) \u2192 GND ... `BS1` (pin 11) \u2192 VCC ... `BS2` (pin 12) \u2192 GND. That BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 strapping ... is the SSD1306's documented I2C-mode pin configuration\"}, {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"display.kicad_sch (Sheet /DISPLAY/): BS0 pin 10 wire runs up to a horizontal bus labelled VCC, which also carries the junctions for R4, R6 and R7 pull-ups\"}], \"impact\": \"With BS0 high, the SSD1306 interface-mode strapping no longer matches I2C. The display may not respond on the DISP_SCL/DISP_SDA bus, leaving the OLED blank or non-functional.\", \"confidence\": 0.6}], \"summary\": \"The display sheet ties SSD1306 BS0 (pin 10) to the VCC bus instead of GND as the specification requires, which changes the interface-mode strapping away from I2C. The rest of the drawing matches the specification.\"}",
